cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "pyrulearn"
type: software
version: 0.2.0
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/juffif/pyrulearn"
abstract: >-
  pyrulearn is a Python library for representing, learning, combining and
  analyzing propositional rule models over Boolean data: native rule learners
  (separate-and-conquer families such as CN2, PFOIL, FOSSIL and Pypper, a RIPPER re-implementation,
  with removal or weighted covering; locally optimal rules; the associative
  classifiers CBA, CMAR, CPAR and IDS; the rule ensembles SLIPPER, LRI, ENDER,
  BOOMER and optimal rule boosting; and RuleFit) and interfaces to external
  ones (scikit-learn, wittgenstein, imodels, Weka, LORD, pyarc, mlrl-boomer,
  realkd).
keywords:
  - rule learning
  - interpretable machine learning
  - association rules
  - decision lists
authors:
  - family-names: Fürnkranz
    given-names: Johannes
    email: juffi@faw.jku.at
    affiliation: "Johannes Kepler University Linz"
